    "readerOrReportLog": [
      "You see a fishing weir (gapped).\n\nNEEDS REPAIR\nThe weir's stakes have rotted at the waterline; the perch go round it.\n\nLasting repair\n- 2 salvaged timber (used)\n- 2 oak haft (used)\nTools and machines\n- hatchet (kept)\n\nTemporary patch (about 150 turns)\n- 1 salvaged timber (used)\nTools and machines\nNone required.\n\nHow to use: Stand beside it, press C and choose mend the fishing weir for good, or patch it for now. The menu lists each material with how many you carry.\nNeeds: to mend it for good: 2 salvaged timber, 2 oak haft (and a hatchet to work with); to patch it for now: 1 salvaged timber.\nCost and limits: Mending uses up the materials and keeps any tool, and the repair lasts. A patch holds about 150 turns, then fails.\nRight now you cannot: mend the fishing weir for good (You still need 2 salvaged timber, 2 oak haft and a hatchet to work with (it is not used up)), patch the fishing weir for now (You still need 1 salvaged timber).\n\nA line of oak stakes driven across the shallows with a gap woven in for the fish to be driven toward. The perch run along it, or round it when it fails.",
      "Quest accepted: The Gapped Weir.",
      "You see a fishing weir (gapped).\nConcord repair booked. Due on day 2 at Dusk.\n\nA line of oak stakes driven across the shallows with a gap woven in for the fish to be driven toward. The perch run along it, or round it when it fails."
    ]
  },
